1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. Nf3 Nc6 4. d4 exd4 5. Nd5 Nxe4 6. Bc4 Be7 7. Nxd4 $1 ({
Theory gives only} 7. O-O O-O {when White's compensation is insufficient.})
7... O-O 8. Nb5 $1 {This leads to wild complications which Kenworthy and his
club colleagues at London Centymca have analysed in depth.} Bb4+ 9. c3 Nxf2 10.
Qh5 $1 ({Hoping for} 10. Kxf2 $2 Qh4+) 10... Nxh1 11. cxb4 Nxb4 {Another
tactical shot (12 Nxb4 Qe7+) but White is ready.} ({Stockfish 14 (2021) finds} 
11... Re8+ $3 12. Kf1 Re5 {when White's tactical tricks don't work and Black
wins. It turns out that White's 10 Kxf2? was actually 10 Kxf2! - objectively
the best move. JS}) 12. Bg5 $1 Re8+ 13. Kf1 Re5 (13... f6 14. Nxf6+ {is
hopeless}) ({while if} 13... g6 14. Qh4 {wins.}) 14. Re1 $1 {Sources: bulletin;
The Guardian, 19 December 1981; BCM, April 1982, p150} (14. Re1 {For if} Rxe1+
(14... Rxg5 15. Qxg5 $1) 15. Kxe1 Qe8+ 16. Ne7+ Kf8 (16... Kh8 17. Bxf7) 17.
Nxc7 {. An elegant miniature destined for a world tour of chess magazines,
columns and anthologies.}) 1-0

